# Platform stack (Spring Boot 3.5.7 BOM)

| Component | Version / source |
|-----------|------------------|
| Java | 17 |
| Spring Boot | 3.5.x (`spring-boot-starter-parent`) |
| MongoDB driver | `mongodb-driver-sync` 5.5.x (via `spring-boot-starter-data-mongodb`) |
| Redis client | Jedis 6.x (explicit `jedis` dependency — not Lettuce) |
| Artemis client | `artemis-jakarta-client` 2.40.x (via `spring-boot-starter-artemis`) |
| MongoDB / Redis / Artemis servers | Platform deployment — confirm with ops/helm, not pinned in service `pom.xml` |

Do not bump client libraries independently; align with the Spring Boot parent BOM unless platform team approves.

# Dependencies

| Tech | Use | Do NOT use |
|------|-----|------------|
| Mongo | `spring-boot-starter-data-mongodb` | Raw `MongoClient` in services |
| Redis | `jedis` + `spring-boot-starter-data-redis` | Lettuce, Redisson |
| JMS | `spring-boot-starter-artemis` | RabbitMQ, Kafka clients |

# Connection Architecture

Config classes expose Spring beans; beans delegate to client managers (`MongoClientManager`, `RedisClientManager`, `ActiveMqManager`). Never create connections outside these managers. `VaultLeaseManager` orchestrates credential renewal for all three.

# MongoDB

- Config: `MongoConfig` — `@EnableMongoRepositories`, `MongoTemplate`, `TenantAwareMongoDatabaseFactory`
- Client: `MongoClientManager` — SSL, replica set, `refreshMongoClient()`
- Properties: `spring.data.mongodb.*` + `mongodb.custom.ssl.*` / `mongodb.custom.replicaset.*`
- Repositories: extend `MongoRepository<Entity, String>`; entities in `model/*Entity` with `@Document`
- Custom search: interface + `*RepositoryImpl` extending `AbstractMongoSearchRepository` with `MongoFilterBuilder`
- Multi-tenancy: DB selected from `MDC.get(Constants.TENANT_ID)` — set tenant context before DB calls
- Recovery: `MongoDbExceptionRecoveryAspect` triggers credential renewal

# Redis

- Config: `RedisConfig` — beans: `Pool<Jedis>`, `DelegatingRedisConnectionFactory`, `StringRedisTemplate`
- Client: `RedisClientManager` — sentinel/SSL support, `refreshRedisClients()`
- Properties: `spring.redis.*` via `RedisProperties`
- Jedis pool (primary): `try (Jedis jedis = jedisPool.getResource())` + `RedisRepository` for RedisJSON ops
- `StringRedisTemplate`: distributed locks via `RedisDistributedLockRegistry`
- Cache impls: `*CacheImpl` in `repository/` — inject `Pool<Jedis>`, use transactions/pipelines for atomic updates
- Recovery: `RedisExceptionRecoveryAspect`

# Artemis / JMS

- Config: `JmsConfig` — `CredentialRotationConnectionFactory` wrapping `ActiveMQConnectionFactory`
- Client: `ActiveMqManager` — stops/restarts listeners on credential rotation
- Properties: `spring.artemis.*` + `amq.*` via `ActivemqProperties`
- Publish: `JmsPublisher` / `ActivemqPublisher` — `JmsTemplate` with `setPubSubDomain(true)`, JSON `TextMessage`, set `JMSType` + tenant/correlation JMS properties
- Subscribe: `@JmsListener` with durable shared subscription, `containerFactory` from `JmsConfig`, `CLIENT_ACKNOWLEDGE`
- Recovery: `ActiveMqExceptionRecoveryAspect`

# Vault / Credentials

- `VaultLeaseManager` orchestrates renewal for all three backends
- Prod: static passwords left empty; Vault provides dynamic creds
- Do not hardcode credentials; use existing property prefixes

# Anti-patterns

- Do not add Lettuce, Redisson, or alternate Redis drivers
- Do not create `new MongoClient()` / `new JedisPool()` / `new ActiveMQConnectionFactory()` outside client managers
- Do not add `@EnableJms` manually (Artemis auto-config handles it)
- Do not add new JMS listeners without a `containerFactory` bean from `JmsConfig`
